<title>GREECE: Greece signs 36bln drachma loan facility with EIB.</title>
<headline>Greece signs 36bln drachma loan facility with EIB.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece signed a 20-year, 36 billion drachma loan with the European Investment Bank (EIB) to partly finance the construction of a major highway linking Athens with the northern Greek-Bulgarian border, the national economy ministry said.</p>
<p>The loan has a five-year grace period and carries an interest rate of 3.98 percent, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;The loan is also expected to receive an interest rate subsidy of 2.0 percent from the financing arm of the European Economic Area.&quot;</p>
<p>The loan facility was signed today by deputy National Economy Minister Christos Pachtas and EIB vice-president Panayiotis Yennimatas.</p>
<p>The cost of the highway is budgeted at 89.01 billion drachmas. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
